WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.700
Oxford Bookworms Library, Starter. The Mystery of Manor Hall by Jane Cammack. Read by David Thorpe. 

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:17.800
Published and copyright Oxford University Press 2013. 

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:46.900
The Mystery of Manor Hall. 

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:53.100
We don’t want to stay with Uncle Henry, Mum! 

00:00:53.200 --> 00:01:01.700
The boy with dark hair and blue eyes takes his mobile phone out of his pocket.

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:07.925
Grandma says he doesn't like teenagers.

00:01:07.985 --> 00:01:14.830
His mother shakes her head and Tom looks out the window again.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:17.692
The car goes left.

00:01:17.752 --> 00:01:23.082
The sign on the gate says Manor Hall.

00:01:23.142 --> 00:01:31.012
Manor Hall, says the beautiful girl sitting next to her brother Tom.

00:01:31.072 --> 00:01:35.564
Does Uncle Henry live here?

00:01:35.624 --> 00:01:40.406
Her mother hears what Milly says.

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:46.768
Henry is strange, but he's nice too.

00:01:46.828 --> 00:01:51.890
Can't we come to the new house with you, Mum?

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:55.600
We can help. Milly asks.
  
00:01:55.660 --> 00:02:00.397
No, Milly, says her mum.

00:02:00.457 --> 00:02:05.298
There aren't any beds in the new house.

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:08.339
The car stops.

00:02:08.398 --> 00:02:12.419
Here we are, says Mum.

00:02:12.479 --> 00:02:17.250
The house is very old and dark.

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:20.781
There are lots of small windows.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:24.039
Milly is afraid.

00:02:24.099 --> 00:02:27.668
A man opens the door.

00:02:27.728 --> 00:02:34.229
He is old, and he has got white hair and big eyebrows.

00:02:34.289 --> 00:02:40.760
He looks at Tom and Milly with his grey eyes.

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:45.072
You’re late, he says.

00:02:45.132 --> 00:02:47.492
Come in.

00:02:47.552 --> 00:02:51.000
Sorry, says Tom.

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:53.234
I’m Tom.

00:02:53.294 --> 00:02:55.717
How do you do?

00:02:55.777 --> 00:02:59.541
The old man looks angry.

00:02:59.601 --> 00:03:03.953
And I’m Milly, says Milly.

00:03:04.012 --> 00:03:08.024
Your house is very big.

00:03:08.084 --> 00:03:12.655
It is, says Uncle Henry.

00:03:12.715 --> 00:03:21.132
You can explore, but there is one room where you can’t go.

00:03:21.192 --> 00:03:32.784
They walk along a corridor and see a sitting room where there are beautiful sofas and pictures on the walls.

00:03:32.844 --> 00:03:36.537
Then they come to a door.

00:03:36.597 --> 00:03:43.712
This is the music room, says Uncle Henry.

00:03:43.772 --> 00:03:46.895
There is a sign on the door.

00:03:46.955 --> 00:03:51.592
It says DO NOT ENTER.

00:03:51.652 --> 00:03:56.578
Why can’t we go in there? asks Milly.
 
00:03:56.638 --> 00:04:02.192
I can play the piano, and I love music.

00:04:02.252 --> 00:04:06.144
Uncle Henry shakes his head.

00:04:06.204 --> 00:04:14.450
I can’t tell you, but never open this door.

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:18.932
What a strange man!

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:22.700
Tom says when they are in their bedroom. 

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:26.985
Why can’t we go into the music room?

00:04:27.045 --> 00:04:29.978
But Milly isn't listening.

00:04:30.037 --> 00:04:34.552
Let’s explore, she says.

00:04:34.612 --> 00:04:40.977
Tom and Milly walk up and down and open doors.

00:04:41.037 --> 00:04:44.740
Then they come to the music room.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:50.951
Tom is about to open the door when Uncle Henry sees them.

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:54.007
Get away from there!

00:04:54.067 --> 00:04:56.738
shouts Uncle Henry.

00:04:56.797 --> 00:05:06.950
Later, when they are having dinner in the dining room, Uncle Henry is very quiet.

00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:11.922
Are you angry with us? asks Milly.
 
00:05:11.982 --> 00:05:15.232
Uncle Henry doesn't answer.

00:05:15.292 --> 00:05:17.578
He shakes his head.

00:05:17.638 --> 00:05:24.536
Then he says, There’s a full moon tonight.

00:05:24.595 --> 00:05:28.946
He gets up and looks out the window.

00:05:29.006 --> 00:05:37.650
Lock your bedroom door, he says, and don’t open it.

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:43.452
I don’t understand, Milly says to Tom.

00:05:43.512 --> 00:05:47.900
Why does Uncle Henry look at the moon?

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:51.788
Why can’t we go into the music room?

00:05:51.848 --> 00:05:54.710
It’s a mystery.

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:57.521
Tom isn't listening.

00:05:57.581 --> 00:05:59.852
He's reading a book.

00:05:59.912 --> 00:06:04.844
I want to explore, Tom says suddenly.

00:06:04.904 --> 00:06:09.436
We can’t, says Milly.

00:06:09.496 --> 00:06:14.258
It's midnight, and Milly wakes up.

00:06:14.318 --> 00:06:17.141
It's very dark in the bedroom.

00:06:17.201 --> 00:06:19.934
And she can hear a noise.

00:06:19.994 --> 00:06:25.086
She gets out of bed and goes to her brother's bed.

00:06:25.146 --> 00:06:32.001
Tom? Tom, she says, and shakes his arm.
 
00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:35.232
Tom opens his eyes.

00:06:35.292 --> 00:06:39.314
Milly, it’s late.

00:06:39.374 --> 00:06:42.606
Go back to bed.

00:06:42.666 --> 00:06:46.181
He closes his eyes again.

00:06:46.241 --> 00:06:50.466
No! Tom! Get up!
  
00:06:50.526 --> 00:06:53.966
There’s a strange noise.

00:06:54.026 --> 00:06:58.437
Tom goes to the door and listens.

00:06:58.497 --> 00:07:02.538
You’re right, he says to Milly.

00:07:02.598 --> 00:07:07.168
I can hear someone singing.

00:07:07.228 --> 00:07:13.818
Can Uncle Henry sing? Milly asks Tom.
 
00:07:13.878 --> 00:07:18.018
Tom laughs. Let’s see.
 
00:07:18.078 --> 00:07:20.388
He opens the door.

00:07:20.448 --> 00:07:25.762
No, Milly says. There’s a full moon.
 
00:07:25.822 --> 00:07:28.674
We can’t go out.

00:07:28.734 --> 00:07:36.228
You can stay here, but I want to see who’s singing at midnight.

00:07:36.288 --> 00:07:43.211
Tom opens the door and they run into the corridor.

00:07:43.271 --> 00:07:50.356
Someone is singing in the music room, says Milly.

00:07:50.416 --> 00:07:53.608
You’re right, says Tom.

00:07:53.667 --> 00:08:00.504
It’s a man, and he’s singing a song about the sea.

00:08:00.564 --> 00:08:04.928
It’s beautiful, says Milly.

00:08:04.987 --> 00:08:08.281
Is it Uncle Henry?

00:08:08.341 --> 00:08:11.936
Tom isn't listening.

00:08:11.996 --> 00:08:17.231
He opens the door of the music room and goes in.

00:08:17.451 --> 00:08:20.312
Don’t, Tom, says Milly.

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:26.524
We can’t go into the music room.

00:08:26.583 --> 00:08:32.775
The music room is very big and Milly is afraid.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:42.574
We haven’t got much time before Uncle Henry hears us, she says.

00:08:42.634 --> 00:08:48.163
Tom puts the light on and the singing stops.

00:08:48.223 --> 00:08:55.318
In the music room there's a piano and there are lots of pictures on the wall.

00:08:55.378 --> 00:08:58.720
But Uncle Henry isn't there.

00:08:58.781 --> 00:09:02.543
Milly wants to go.

00:09:02.603 --> 00:09:09.034
On one wall there is a very big picture of a ship.

00:09:09.094 --> 00:09:17.164
Milly and Tom look at the picture and they can see that the sea is moving.

00:09:17.224 --> 00:09:20.796
They can hear the water.

00:09:20.856 --> 00:09:25.058
There is a man standing on the ship.

00:09:25.118 --> 00:09:30.070
He has got long black hair and a black hat.

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:33.992
He is singing a song about the sea.

00:09:34.052 --> 00:09:37.105
He’s a pirate!

00:09:37.165 --> 00:09:42.950
Tom and Milly are afraid, but they can't move.

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:45.600
The pirate looks at them.

00:09:45.732 --> 00:09:49.655
He stops singing, and he smiles.

00:09:49.715 --> 00:09:57.002
Suddenly, he comes out of the picture and into the music room.

00:09:57.062 --> 00:10:01.084
Help! shouts Milly.
 
00:10:01.144 --> 00:10:05.734
Milly looks at the handsome pirate.

00:10:05.794 --> 00:10:13.034
He has a big hat, and he is very white.

00:10:13.094 --> 00:10:22.168
He’s a ghost, she says in a quiet voice to Tom.

00:10:22.228 --> 00:10:26.871
Tom, let’s go!

00:10:26.931 --> 00:10:30.402
Tom doesn't answer.

00:10:30.462 --> 00:10:36.609
The pirate is near the door, so they can't go.

00:10:36.669 --> 00:10:42.555
Who’s in my music room?

00:10:42.616 --> 00:10:49.291
the pirate shouts. This is my room!

00:10:49.351 --> 00:10:53.414
You’re right, says Tom.

00:10:53.474 --> 00:11:00.589
This is your music room, and we’re going to bed.

00:11:00.649 --> 00:11:04.400
The pirate shakes his head.

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:11.996
Oh no, you’re not. Sit down.
 
00:11:12.056 --> 00:11:18.838
I’m going to tell you my story.

00:11:18.898 --> 00:11:31.156
My name is William Bones, but everyone calls me Billy, says the pirate.

00:11:31.216 --> 00:11:36.650
The year is 1793.

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:46.870
My men and I sail the seven seas in my ship, the Pearl.

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:56.506
We fight pirate ships and we sing songs about the sea.

00:11:56.566 --> 00:12:00.441
We are very happy

00:12:00.501 --> 00:12:06.138
because we have lots of treasure.

00:12:06.198 --> 00:12:20.006
Then one day I help an old woman, and she paints a picture of my ship.

00:12:20.066 --> 00:12:26.165
This picture’s magic, she tells me.

00:12:26.225 --> 00:12:34.186
Before you die, put it in a house near the sea.

00:12:34.246 --> 00:12:45.914
When you die and the moon is full, your ghost can sail your ship for one night.

00:12:45.974 --> 00:12:57.156
Then the old woman looks at me and she says, ‘Pirate Billy Bones!’

00:12:57.216 --> 00:13:05.767
Remember that the picture must be near the sea.

00:13:05.827 --> 00:13:13.798
Now it’s 1850, Billy says.

00:13:13.858 --> 00:13:22.184
When I’m old, I die in my house by the sea.

00:13:22.244 --> 00:13:26.368
The old woman is right.

00:13:26.428 --> 00:13:36.074
When the moon is full, my ghost can sail my ship for one night.

00:13:36.134 --> 00:13:49.000
But then, in 1910, someone brings the picture here to Manor Hall.

00:13:49.060 --> 00:14:01.328
The pirate says, This house isn’t near the sea, so I can’t sail my ship.

00:14:01.388 --> 00:14:08.912
When the moon is full, I sing songs about the sea.

00:14:08.972 --> 00:14:14.054
And the people in the house are afraid.

00:14:14.114 --> 00:14:18.387
They are afraid of the ghost.

00:14:18.446 --> 00:14:27.058
They put my picture in the music room and lock the door.

00:14:27.118 --> 00:14:33.070
Suddenly, the door of the music room opens.

00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:36.230
Uncle Henry stands there.

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:42.782
He looks at Billy Bones and then at Tom and Milly.

00:14:42.842 --> 00:14:46.214
His face is white.

00:14:46.274 --> 00:14:50.928
Oh dear, he says.

00:14:50.988 --> 00:14:56.722
Now you know about the mystery.

00:14:56.782 --> 00:15:05.658
Now I must tell you my story, says Uncle Henry.

00:15:05.718 --> 00:15:11.300
The year is 1976.

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:16.300
I buy this house from an old man.

00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:23.998
He tells me about the picture and the ghost in the music room.

00:15:24.058 --> 00:15:30.791
I’m afraid of ghosts, and I don’t go into the music room.

00:15:30.851 --> 00:15:33.882
I lock the door.

00:15:33.942 --> 00:15:38.750
Every month, when there is a full moon, 

00:15:38.810 --> 00:15:47.167
I hear a pirate singing songs about the sea, says Uncle Henry.

00:15:47.227 --> 00:15:50.700
I know that he is unhappy, 

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:56.009
and I know that he wants to go back to the sea.

00:15:56.069 --> 00:16:02.191
But I’m afraid, and I can’t help him.

00:16:02.251 --> 00:16:05.700
I know, says Tom.

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:13.794
Our new house is in a beautiful place near the sea, he says.

00:16:13.854 --> 00:16:20.578
From my bedroom, I can hear the seagulls and the waves.

00:16:20.638 --> 00:16:22.900
Come with us.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:30.744
We can put your picture in the breakfast room where you can see the sea.

00:16:30.804 --> 00:16:35.028
Uncle Henry begins to smile.

00:16:35.088 --> 00:16:42.412
How wonderful! says Billy Bones.

00:16:42.472 --> 00:16:51.620
I’m happy that you want to go with Tom and Milly, says Uncle Henry.

00:16:51.680 --> 00:16:58.397
Please sit down, Billy Bones, and listen.

00:16:58.457 --> 00:17:03.191
Everyone sits at the kitchen table.

00:17:03.251 --> 00:17:09.612
You can go, but you must be quiet.

00:17:09.673 --> 00:17:15.910
You must sing quietly in their new house.

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:20.892
All right, says Billy Bones.

00:17:20.951 --> 00:17:26.884
Are you afraid of ghosts now, Henry?

00:17:26.944 --> 00:17:29.315
Henry smiles.

00:17:29.375 --> 00:17:34.466
No, I’m not, Billy.

00:17:34.526 --> 00:17:38.562
Mum’s here, says Milly.

00:17:38.623 --> 00:17:41.488
They run out of the house.

00:17:41.548 --> 00:17:49.412
Mum, we have something from Uncle Henry, says Milly.

00:17:49.472 --> 00:17:53.194
It’s for the new house.

00:17:53.254 --> 00:18:02.400
Mum looks at the picture, a ship, and a handsome pirate.

00:18:02.460 --> 00:18:07.215
How lovely, says Mum.

00:18:07.275 --> 00:18:13.362
Tom and Milly say goodbye to Uncle Henry.

00:18:13.422 --> 00:18:18.696
They take the picture to their new house by the sea.

00:18:18.756 --> 00:18:27.020
Pirate Billy Bones stands on his ship and he looks at his new home.

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:34.866
He can hear seagulls and he quietly sings a song about the sea.

00:18:34.926 --> 00:18:43.000
One day, when there is a full moon, his ship disappears.